# Template for `local.env` — the local production-style run.
#
#   cp local.env.example local.env   # then fill in real values
#   docker compose --env-file local.env up --build
#
# ###########################################################################
# # DUPLICATION WARNING — read before editing                               #
# #                                                                         #
# # This file and `dev.env.example` are each SELF-CONTAINED: both carry the #
# # complete variable set, including INTERNAL_TOKEN and every RDM_*_API_KEY.#
# # The same secrets therefore live in TWO places (`local.env` and          #
# # `dev.env`), and they WILL drift if you only update one of them. When    #
# # you rotate a key or change a credential, change it in BOTH files.       #
# #                                                                         #
# # This is the accepted cost of the two-file split: it buys env files that #
# # need no layering and a mode switch that is just `--env-file <file>`.    #
# ###########################################################################
#
# ONE-TIME LOCAL SETUP — schedule-sftp host keys
#
# Unlike every other credential in this file, `schedule-sftp`'s SSH host
# keys are NOT an env var: the service bind-mounts them from a host
# directory (docker-compose.yml's `./schedule-sftp-host-keys:/srv/sftpgo/host_keys:ro`),
# the local-dev stand-in for the Helm chart's chart-generated Secret. Before
# the first `docker compose ... up` that includes `schedule-sftp`, generate
# them once (git-ignored — see .gitignore — never commit them):
#   mkdir -p schedule-sftp-host-keys
#   ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f schedule-sftp-host-keys/ssh_host_ed25519_key -N ""
#
# NONE of the RDM_*_BASE_URL values below are real Rail Data Marketplace
# endpoints. They are deliberately non-functional placeholders
# (`*.example.invalid`, which is reserved by RFC 2606 and guaranteed to
# never resolve) so this file can't be mistaken later for a real
# configuration. As of this plan's completion, none of the following gaps
# have been resolved with real RDM account data:
#   - Incidents feed: no confirmed base URL/endpoint path.
#   - TOCs feed: no confirmed base URL/endpoint path.
#   - Exact `x-apikey` auth header name: corroborated only via a different
#     RDM product's documented example, not proven for these three feeds.
#   - Stations feed JSON field casing: unconfirmed (see
#     crates/poller-stations/src/schema.rs).
#   - LDBWS (Live Departure Board) feed: no confirmed base URL/product-slug
#     segment; two variants seen in research, not reconciled.
#   - LDBWS feed rate limit: one low-confidence source claims a number,
#     not corroborated against RDM's own plan/quota page.
# Fill in the real values only once you have an actual RDM account and have
# confirmed each endpoint against the live API.
#
# Consequence for a first run: the four pollers will fail against these
# placeholder hosts and restart in a loop. That is expected, not a
# regression — postgres, api, aggregator and frontend all come up fine.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compose wiring
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which YAML files `docker compose` loads. Compose reads COMPOSE_FILE out of
# the file passed to `--env-file` before it resolves the model, which is
# what lets a single `--env-file local.env` select the whole mode. This
# (production-style) mode is the base file alone — no dev override, so
# release build args and `runtime-prod` / `next start` for the frontend.
COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# postgres
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
POSTGRES_USER=distant_signal
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme-local-dev-only
POSTGRES_DB=distant_signal

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# api (crates/api/src/data/config.rs: ServiceArguments)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL and BIND_URL are assembled in docker-compose.yml from the
# postgres vars above / a fixed in-container bind address, so they aren't
# repeated here. API_HOST_PORT controls the host-side port mapping only.
API_HOST_PORT=8080

# Shared secret every poller must present via the `X-Internal-Token` header
# to reach the api's /private/* ingestion endpoints (crates/api/src/auth.rs).
# Must not be empty — the api refuses to start with an empty token.
INTERNAL_TOKEN=changeme-shared-secret-local-dev-only

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OIDC SSO configuration (crates/api/src/data/config.rs: ServiceArguments)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Point at a real or locally-run OIDC-compliant SSO server (e.g. Keycloak,
# Authentik, Authelia). All fields are required.
SSO_ISSUER_URL=http://sso.example.invalid
SSO_CLIENT_ID=changeme-sso-client-id
SSO_CLIENT_SECRET=changeme-sso-client-secret
SSO_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback
SSO_POST_LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:3000/
SESSION_TTL_DAYS=14

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# poller-incidents (crates/poller-incidents/src/config.rs: Config)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GAP: RSPS5050 P-03-00 Rev A §10 does not publish an endpoint path for this
# product. Placeholder only — replace with the real feed base URL once known.
RDM_INCIDENTS_BASE_URL=http://rdm-incidents.example.invalid
RDM_INCIDENTS_API_KEY=changeme-rdm-incidents-api-key
# Recommended cadence per spec is 300s (5 min); see dev.env.example for the
# shortened values used when verifying the poll loop locally.
POLL_INTERVAL_SECS_INCIDENTS=300

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# poller-stations (crates/poller-stations/src/config.rs: Config)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Confirmed path suffix per spec is `/stations`; the poller appends it
# itself. Host portion is account-specific — placeholder only.
RDM_STATIONS_BASE_URL=http://rdm-stations.example.invalid
RDM_STATIONS_API_KEY=changeme-rdm-stations-api-key
# Recommended cadence per spec is 86400s (24h, "once per day, overnight").
POLL_INTERVAL_SECS_STATIONS=86400

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# poller-tocs (crates/poller-tocs/src/config.rs: Config)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GAP: RSPS5050 P-03-00 Rev A §3 does not publish an endpoint path for this
# product in the current spec edition. Placeholder only.
RDM_TOCS_BASE_URL=http://rdm-tocs.example.invalid
RDM_TOCS_API_KEY=changeme-rdm-tocs-api-key
# Recommended cadence per spec is 86400s (24h, "at least once every 24
# hours").
POLL_INTERVAL_SECS_TOCS=86400

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# poller-ldbws (crates/poller-ldbws/src/config.rs: Config)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GAP: the exact RDM product-slug segment for the Live Departure Board
# product is unconfirmed — two variants were found during research
# (e.g. "1010-live-departure-board-dep" vs "...-dep1_2"). Placeholder only;
# confirm the real value once you have RDM account access.
LDBWS_BASE_URL=http://rdm-ldbws.example.invalid
LDBWS_API_KEY=changeme-rdm-ldbws-api-key
# Services requested per station per poll (LDBWS's own default is 10).
LDBWS_NUM_ROWS=10
# Target cadence per DESIGN.md is 30-60s; this feed's real rate limit is
# unconfirmed, so 60 (the conservative end) is the default.
POLL_INTERVAL_SECS_LDBWS=60

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# poller-tfl (crates/poller-tfl/src/config.rs: Config)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No GAP here: TfL's Unified API is public and documented, so the default in
# the binary is the real endpoint. Register at api-portal.tfl.gov.uk for a
# subscription key; the free tier is documented at ~500 requests/min, which
# one request every 300s is nowhere near.
TFL_BASE_URL=https://api.tfl.gov.uk
TFL_APP_KEY=changeme-tfl-subscription-key
# Line-status-only scope: no bus/river-bus/cable-car, and no national-rail
# (this app's own four pollers cover that far better than TfL's summary).
TFL_MODES=tube,dlr,overground,elizabeth-line,tram
# TfL publishes no recommended cadence; 300s mirrors poller-incidents.
POLL_INTERVAL_SECS_TFL=300

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# aggregator (crates/aggregator/src/config.rs: Config)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Target cadence per DESIGN.md is 30-60s; 60 is the default.
POLL_INTERVAL_SECS_AGGREGATOR=60
# How long line_status_history rows are kept before being pruned. Read by
# BOTH the aggregator (which enforces it) and the api service (which only
# reports it, via /public/history-retention, so the frontend's history
# range picker can be honest about it) -- keep this one value, don't split
# it into two.
HISTORY_RETENTION_DAYS=7

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# notifier (crates/notifier/src/config.rs: Config) -- Web Push for
# pinned-line/tracked-train notifications. Required by the notifier
# service with no default; left unset here (docker-compose.yml defaults
# each to an empty string) means the whole stack still starts, but
# notifier itself fails fast and crash-loops until these are set -- see
# crates/notifier/src/main.rs's startup `ensure!`s. Generate a real VAPID
# keypair with:
#   openssl ecparam -genkey -name prime256v1 -noout -out vapid_private.pem
# then derive the public key per the web-push crate's own documented
# process. VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY is also read by the api service (above) to
# serve GET /public/notifications/vapid-public-key -- same value both
# places.
POLL_INTERVAL_SECS_NOTIFIER=60
COOLDOWN_MINUTES_NOTIFIER=20
TRAIN_DELAY_THRESHOLD_MINUTES_NOTIFIER=15
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:admin@example.invalid
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# enricher (crates/enricher/src/config.rs: Config)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REDIS_URL is fixed to the in-network `redis://redis:6379` in
# docker-compose.yml, not overridden here.
# crates/enricher/src/config.rs -- point at your own OpenAI-compatible
# endpoint (local server or hosted provider). No vendor is assumed.
LLM_BASE_URL=http://llm.example.invalid/v1
LLM_API_KEY=
# Model recommendation (2026-08-21 live-eval battery against a real
# self-hosted Ollama endpoint -- see
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-20-incident-nlp-extraction-design.md's
# "Live-eval results" section for the full comparison and methodology):
# gemma3:12b was the most reliable candidate tested -- correct multi-period
# segmentation, correctly resisted an over-segmentation trap, and was the
# only model with zero dropped/flipped fields across repeated identical
# calls. gpt-oss:20b is a reasonable fallback (slower, more run-to-run
# variance). Smaller models (qwen3.5:4b and under) were unreliable on this
# task in that eval -- your own model/backend may differ, so re-run that
# battery before trusting a different choice in production.
LLM_MODEL=replace-with-your-model-name
# Per-request LLM call timeout -- raise if extractions are timing out
# against a slow/remote server. If you raise this, raise
# RECLAIM_MIN_IDLE_SECS too (see its comment below): default shown.
# LLM_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECS=300
SWEEP_INTERVAL_SECS=3600
# Debounced retry for a timed-out/failed extraction -- defaults shown.
# Keep RECLAIM_MIN_IDLE_SECS comfortably above 3 * LLM_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECS
# (one incident makes three sequential LLM calls).
# RECLAIM_INTERVAL_SECS=60
# RECLAIM_MIN_IDLE_SECS=1000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# trust-consumer (crates/trust-consumer/src/config.rs: Config)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GAP: none of these are confirmed against a live RDM Train Movements
# catalogue entry. Requires the RDM subscription/licence prerequisites in
# docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-28-train-tracking.md to be completed
# before these can be real values.
KAFKA_BROKERS=kafka.example.invalid:9094
KAFKA_TOPIC=replace-with-confirmed-topic-name
KAFKA_CONSUMER_GROUP=distant-signal-trust-consumer
KAFKA_SASL_USERNAME=changeme-rdm-trust-consumer-key
KAFKA_SASL_PASSWORD=changeme-rdm-trust-consumer-secret
KAFKA_SASL_MECHANISM=PLAIN
REFERENCE_RELOAD_SECS=60
RETENTION_DAYS_TRAIN_EVENTS=90

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# schedule-sftp + schedule-ingest (crates/schedule-ingest/src/config.rs:
# Config) -- CIF SCHEDULE feed (SFTP push). See
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-01-schedule-feed-push-design.md and
# docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-01-schedule-feed-push-ingestion.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This app mints this account, not DTD -- these values are this app's own
# choice, communicated to DTD once push configuration is confirmed
# reachable (still a GAP -- see the plan's Task 1), not something to look
# up from an external system. The Helm chart auto-generates and preserves
# a random password instead of defaulting it (see values.yaml's
# scheduleFeed.sftp.password); Compose has no equivalent generation
# mechanism, so this is a real (arbitrary, low-stakes for local dev)
# default -- change it before actually giving these details to DTD.
SCHEDULE_SFTP_USERNAME=dtd-push
# Never commit a REAL password here -- same rule as every other secret in
# this file. This default is a placeholder for local dev only.
SCHEDULE_SFTP_PASSWORD=changeme-local-dev-password
# Host-side port mapping for the SFTP listener only; the in-container port
# is fixed to 2022 in docker-compose.yml.
SCHEDULE_SFTP_PORT=2222
# The folder DTD's account lands files in. CORRECTED 2026-09-01 (this
# task): this account's SFTP home/chroot directory is now set to exactly
# /data/schedule-feed/<this value> (see docker/schedule-sftp-entrypoint.sh),
# so DTD's push client actually sees itself uploading to "/" once
# connected -- "incoming" here just names where that lands on this app's
# own filesystem, not a subfolder DTD navigates into. Matches
# charts/distant-signal/templates/schedulefeed-deployment.yaml's
# WATCH_DIR/destinationFolder+folderPath concept, collapsed to one value
# here (append a subfolder directly, e.g. "incoming/2026", rather than a
# separate variable -- see docker-compose.yml's own comment on this).
SCHEDULE_FEED_DESTINATION_PATH=incoming
# Comma-separated HH:MM times, Europe/London -- reused directly from the
# (now-superseded) pull design's Scheduling section: the window describes
# when DTD *produces* the feed, not which party connects.
SCHEDULE_FEED_CHECK_TIMES=22:00,22:30,23:00,23:30,00:00,00:30,01:00,01:30,16:00
# How many complete sequences to retain on disk (current + fallback).
RETENTION_KEEP_SEQUENCES=2
# How many consecutive polling cycles a manifest-listed file's mtime/size
# must be unchanged before it's treated complete -- see the plan's Task 3.
SCHEDULE_FEED_STABILITY_CYCLES=2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# rail-mcp -- opt-in, NOT part of a plain `docker compose up`. See
# docker-compose.yml's `rail-mcp:` service comment and
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-01-train-mcp-integration-design.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This service is gated behind Compose's `profiles: ["rail-mcp"]` -- add
# `--profile rail-mcp` (or set COMPOSE_PROFILES=rail-mcp) to actually start
# it, e.g.:
#   docker compose --env-file local.env --profile rail-mcp up --build
# The variables below still need real (or placeholder) values even though
# the service itself won't start without that flag: Compose interpolates
# every `${VAR}` reference in the whole file before it filters by profile,
# so leaving any of these unset still produces a "variable is not set"
# warning at `docker compose up`/`config` time regardless of whether
# rail-mcp is ever actually activated.
#
# RAIL_MCP_INTERNAL_COMPLETE_TOKEN is the shared secret between the
# rail-mcp service and frontend's own OAuth consent bridge
# (frontend/app/connect-claude/authorize/route.ts) -- mirrors
# INTERNAL_TOKEN's shape above, a distinct credential (they protect
# different processes). UPDATED (embedded-chatbot-shared-foundation-and-
# option-c plan, Task 8): this replaces RAIL_MCP_DISCORD_CLIENT_ID/
# RAIL_MCP_DISCORD_ALLOWED_USER_IDS, which this env file used to document
# here -- the fork's own Discord-OAuth access gate is retired, not kept
# alongside DS's own OIDC-driven adapter (train-mcp design Decision 4d).
RAIL_MCP_INTERNAL_COMPLETE_TOKEN=changeme-rail-mcp-internal-complete-token
# RAIL_MCP_DS_FRONTEND_ORIGIN defaults to http://localhost:${FRONTEND_HOST_PORT:-3000}
# in docker-compose.yml -- override only if you're serving the frontend
# somewhere else in this dev setup.
# LDBWS/Rail Data Marketplace credentials the fork's board/service-detail
# tools call directly (Decision 5 -- not routed through DS's own
# poller-ldbws feed above). Same GAP as poller-ldbws's own
# LDBWS_BASE_URL/LDBWS_API_KEY: base URL and rate limit unconfirmed.
LDBWS_DEPARTURES_URL=http://rdm-ldbws.example.invalid
LDBWS_DEPARTURES_KEY=changeme-rdm-ldbws-departures-key
LDBWS_ARRIVALS_URL=http://rdm-ldbws.example.invalid
LDBWS_ARRIVALS_KEY=changeme-rdm-ldbws-arrivals-key
LDBWS_SERVICE_URL=http://rdm-ldbws.example.invalid
LDBWS_SERVICE_KEY=changeme-rdm-ldbws-service-key
# RAIL_MCP_IMAGE/RAIL_MCP_PORT/RAIL_MCP_PUBLIC_URL/DS_LINE_CATALOGUE_TTL_MS
# all have real defaults in docker-compose.yml's `rail-mcp:` entry, so they
# need no entry here unless you want to override one. RAIL_MCP_IMAGE in
# particular defaults to an intentionally-invalid placeholder
# (ghcr.io/CHANGE-ME/...) that fails loudly ("invalid reference format")
# if this service is ever started via `--profile rail-mcp` without a real
# image configured -- that's deliberate, not a bug; see docker-compose.yml.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# frontend (frontend/lib/api.ts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host-side port mapping only; API_BASE_URL itself is fixed to the
# in-network `http://api:8080` in docker-compose.yml, not overridden here.
FRONTEND_HOST_PORT=3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared across all pollers + api (log verbosity; tracing-subscriber
# EnvFilter syntax, e.g. "info", "poller_stations=debug", "warn").
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUST_LOG=info
